[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
To get started with OpenCloud:

  STORAGE (ZFS):
  OpenCloud relies heavily on filesystem extended attributes (xattr).
  On ZFS it is recommended to create a dedicated dataset with system
  attributes enabled BEFORE the first start, mounted at %%OC_DBDIR%%:

    zfs create -o mountpoint=%%OC_DBDIR%% <your_pool>/opencloud
    zfs set xattr=sa <your_pool>/opencloud

  If the dataset was created before the package was installed, make sure
  the service user owns it:

    chown %%OC_USER%%:%%OC_USER%% %%OC_DBDIR%%
    chmod 0750 %%OC_DBDIR%%

  1. Enable the service:
       sysrc opencloud_enable=YES

  2. Create the initial configuration (prints the admin password once):
       service opencloud init

  3. Put your settings into %%ETCDIR%%/opencloud.env
     (see opencloud.env.sample next to it), then start the service:
       service opencloud start

Data lives in %%OC_DBDIR%%, configuration in %%ETCDIR%%.
The server logs to /var/log/opencloud.log, rotated by newsyslog(8)
(%%PREFIX%%/etc/newsyslog.conf.d/opencloud.conf).

Running behind Caddy or Apache on a sub-domain is described in
%%DOCSDIR%%/README.FreeBSD (installed with the DOCS option).
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  message: <<EOM
After upgrading OpenCloud check whether opencloud.yaml needs changes:

  service opencloud diffconfig

It only shows the differences, nothing is changed. Read the section on
upgrades in %%DOCSDIR%%/README.FreeBSD before using "service opencloud
reconfig", which creates new secrets and passwords.
EOM
}
]
